Restore the child layout margin in the Qt 6 style

Commit fbadbbf3 copied the Qt 5 style to qt6/. Commit a501c957
("PM_DefaultTopLevelMargin, PM_DefaultChildMargin removed") then deleted
the two metrics that Qt 6 dropped and returned 9 pixels for every layout.
The Qt 5 style returns 9 pixels for a window and 6 pixels for a child
layout. Breeze returns 6 pixels for a child layout as well.

Dolphin gives the space widget in its status bar a fixed height, 30 pixels
with the default font. That widget takes the style margin above and below
the free space bar. A 9 pixel margin leaves 12 pixels for the bar. The bar
asks for the font height, 18 pixels with the default font. The label then
almost touches the top and the bottom of the bar.

Restore the Qt 5 logic. Qt 6 has no PM_DefaultTopLevelMargin and no
PM_DefaultChildMargin, so this patch writes the values into the case.

diff --git a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
index 0d3a2fb7..cb030b41 100644
--- a/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
+++ b/qt6/style/qtcurve_api.cpp
@@ -1589,7 +1589,13 @@ Style::pixelMetric(PixelMetric metric, const QStyleOption *option,
     case PM_LayoutTopMargin:
     case PM_LayoutRightMargin:
     case PM_LayoutBottomMargin:
-        return 9;
+        // Qt 6 has no PM_DefaultTopLevelMargin and no PM_DefaultChildMargin.
+        // Keep the Qt 5 values: 9 pixels for a window, 2 for an OpenOffice
+        // widget, 6 for any other child layout.
+        if ((option && (option->state & State_Window)) ||
+            (widget && widget->isWindow()))
+            return 9;
+        return isOOWidget(widget) ? 2 : 6;
     case PM_MenuBarItemSpacing:
         return 0;
     case PM_ToolBarItemMargin:
